=== REFRESH_POLICIES ===
Continuous aggregates (TimescaleDB-managed; refresh policies registered
inline by the up.sql via add_continuous_aggregate_policy):

  cagg_battery_daily    start_offset 30 days   end_offset 1 hour    schedule 1 hour
  cagg_climate_hourly   start_offset 7 days    end_offset 1 hour    schedule 30 minutes
  cagg_signal_hourly    start_offset 30 days   end_offset 1 hour    schedule 1 hour
  cagg_vehicle_daily    start_offset 30 days   end_offset 1 hour    schedule 1 hour

The schedule is the cadence at which the cagg's background refresh job
runs; start_offset / end_offset bound the time range each refresh
incrementally rebuilds. The faster cadence on cagg_climate_hourly
matches the existing legacy precedent in 000147_continuous_aggregates
(climate trend pages are the most latency-sensitive consumer).

Regular materialized views (no TimescaleDB policy; refresh is operational
and must be scheduled by ops). pg_cron is NOT installed in this
deployment (verified by the absence of `pg_cron` from
docker-compose.yml's postgres service); refresh is wired through the
existing maintenance_worker for cagg_fleet_stats already, and ops
should add the remaining four to the same maintenance cycle:

  cagg_fleet_stats         REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY cagg_fleet_stats;
                           Already refreshed by
                           internal/worker/maintenance_worker.go
                           .refreshFleetStats every maintenance cycle.

  cagg_charging_summary    REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY cagg_charging_summary;
                           Suggested cadence: every 1 hour (matches
                           cagg_battery_daily; analytics queries
                           against this MV are not sub-hour-sensitive).

  mv_energy_daily          REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY mv_energy_daily;
                           Suggested cadence: every 1 hour.

  mv_position_hourly       REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY mv_position_hourly;
                           Suggested cadence: every 30 minutes (mirrors
                           cagg_climate_hourly; map / route reads are
                           latency-sensitive).

  mv_signal_stats          REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY mv_signal_stats;
                           Suggested cadence: every 6 hours (signal
                           coverage is an ops-dashboard freshness
                           metric, not a hot read path).

A future phase-42 prompt is expected to extend
internal/worker/maintenance_worker.go .runMaintenance to refresh the
four new MVs alongside the existing cagg_fleet_stats refresh; this
prompt creates the objects only and is not authorized to modify
maintenance_worker.go.

Each regular MV in this file has a UNIQUE INDEX on its grouping
columns so REFRESH CONCURRENTLY works without a non-concurrent first
refresh — verified above by issuing each REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW
CONCURRENTLY against a freshly-created MV in the verify database, all
five returning exit 0.

