  Three pragmatic deviations from the prompt's literal wording, each
  documented inline in the up.sql header:
    D1. cagg_fleet_stats is a regular MV over `drives` (not a cagg
        over `positions`) to preserve the legacy column contract that
        energy_repo.go, regen_handler.go, and maintenance_worker.go
        all query.
    D2. cagg_charging_summary is a regular MV (not a cagg).
        charging_sessions is a non-hypertable per 000171; the cagg_
        prefix matches the in-tree precedent of cagg_fleet_stats.
    D3. cagg_vehicle_daily is sourced from `positions` only (not from
        positions + drives) because cagg invalidation cannot span two
        tables.

  All four real caggs (cagg_battery_daily, cagg_climate_hourly,
  cagg_signal_hourly, cagg_vehicle_daily) get refresh policies via
  add_continuous_aggregate_policy. All five regular MVs get UNIQUE
  INDEXES so REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY works without a
  non-concurrent first refresh; verified end-to-end against a fresh
  TimescaleDB container.

